This fixture exercises phpc's deterministic prepared-statement result-binding
island through a WordPress-shaped `wpdb` object without calling
`mysqli_stmt_store_result()` first. System PHP needs a real initialized
MySQLi/mysqlnd connection and host database row source, while phpc fetches the
current deterministic executed seed-post row directly and leaves
`mysqli_stmt_num_rows()` at the documented pre-buffered value `0`. It does not
implement true by-reference result aliases, arbitrary prepared SQL, real
mysqlnd cursor/network transfer, host database state, PHP warning/error
fidelity, or native database lowering.
